(Bug #70, the range half: a `treating` clause sits between the collection
 and the append separator, so the second `to` that tells a range source
 from a list source was hidden behind it and the sentence did not parse at
 all. Proving the range now reads past the clause.)

(A range source, substituted)
a list called out is [].
append each n from 1 to 3 treating 2 as 99 to out.
print out.

(The control: the same range with no clause still reads as a range)
a list called plain is [].
append each n from 1 to 3 to plain.
print plain.

(And a list source is still a list source, not a range to its destination)
a list called amounts is [10, 20].
a list called copied is [].
append each amount from amounts to copied.
print copied.
